## HEAVY
At most TWO heavy jobs machine-wide across all MPS lanes; for you a heavy job = one full run of the 11-file loop (planned: base once, head once = 2). Take a slot by atomic `mkdir '<project>/.tools/.heavy-lock-1'` (else `-2`; neither free: poll every 60 s), write `holder.txt` (pane name, label, `date`), run ONE job, MOVE the holder file to `.tools/b1517/logs/`, `rmdir` your own dir; never touch another seat's holder (a holder older than 30 minutes with no live pane is REPORTED, never removed). Load gate: `LC_ALL=C uptime` load1 under 24 on TWO reads 120 s apart (not independent: say so). Single-file runs and plants are light. A wait is not a finding; at the hard stop `BLOCKED: heavy lock waiting at load <n>`.

## HOLDS
No PR, no merge, no deploy, **no `az` of any kind**, no hosted call (no HTTP to any host, not even a GET; the exceptions are `gh api -X GET` and the git fetch/push to the repo above), no Jira write, no message to any human, no push of any ref but `b1512/mps-lane-l5-ops-tooling`, no force, no amend of a pushed commit, no reset or rebase, never delete (quarantine to `.tools/b1517/_quarantine/`), no `cd`, no edit of an existing test line, **no new word an operator can see, no new setting, no new status code, no new dependency, no package install**, no run of `deploy-from-ci.sh`, `upload-pricebooks.sh`, `home-probe.sh`, `entra-app-registrations.sh`, `entra_apps.py` or `seed.py --hosted` outside the test files and their fakes/stubs, no `.local/`, no `Source_Documents/**`, no real price store or overlay (every input SYNTHETIC), no read of any `4_Credentials/.azure` content. Shell: absolute single-quoted paths (`!` and a space are in the project path); `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control per count; `${S}:path` with braces in zsh; python `-I -B`; a separator in `echo` is never a bare run of equals signs; every count, `file:line` and clock in STATUS is printed by a program.

